# Copy to .env. Every value is optional: the desk runs with
# market data and news out of the box. Only investigations
# need a language model.

# --- Language model ----------------------------------------
# One word decides where the model runs:
#
#   hosted   development, no GPU: the same model served by
#            NVIDIA. Needs LLM_API_KEY (build.nvidia.com ->
#            the model page -> "Get API Key").
#   local    final recordings and the value proposition: vLLM
#            on the H100s, started with `make llm` (or
#            tunnelled: ssh -L 8000:localhost:8000 user@gpu-box).
#            Prompts never leave the machine.
#
# Before recording on `local`, run `make forget-runs` so no
# explanation produced by the hosted model is replayed.
LLM_PROFILE=local
LLM_API_KEY=

# Rarely needed: any of these overrides its profile default.
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# LLM_MODEL=
# LLM_PROVIDER=
# LLM_WORKERS=

# How reasoning is switched off per request:
#   chat_template  Nemotron 3 / 3.5 (enable_thinking kwarg)
#   system_prompt  Llama-Nemotron   (/no_think)
# If the server refuses the field, the client drops it and
# strips any <think> block from the answer instead.
LLM_THINKING_CONTROL=chat_template

# --- More models: compare explanations ----------------------
# Every investigation is explained by ONE model, chosen in the
# desk. Run the same anomaly through two and the Why view lays
# the ClaimGraphs side by side.
#
# Apertus is the Swiss AI Initiative's fully open model (EPFL,
# ETH Zurich, CSCS). One word decides where it runs:
#
#   local    `make apertus` on the GPU box (port 8001).
#            Default when no key is set. Prompts stay local.
#   hosted   an OpenAI-compatible gateway; needs APERTUS_API_KEY.
#            Default gateway: Public AI (platform.publicai.co).
#            Any other host: set APERTUS_BASE_URL + APERTUS_MODEL,
#            e.g. https://router.huggingface.co/v1 with
#            swiss-ai/Apertus-70B-Instruct-2509 and an HF token.
#   off      do not offer it.
# APERTUS_PROFILE=local
# APERTUS_API_KEY=
# APERTUS_BASE_URL=
# APERTUS_MODEL=
#
# Anything else, as a JSON list. roles: analysis (explains
# anomalies), interaction (Copilot navigation), frontier (a
# second opinion, only when asked for explicitly).
# A third local reader, Nemotron Super 49B, started with
# `make super49b` (check its "model" id with the curl it prints):
# PYTHIA_MODELS=[{"id":"nemotron-super","label":"Nemotron Super 49B","origin":"NVIDIA","provider":"nvidia-nim","model":"nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1.5","base_url":"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1","thinking_control":"system_prompt","timeout_seconds":180,"workers":4}]
# A comparison model that is only used when asked for:
# PYTHIA_MODELS=[{"id":"frontier","label":"Frontier","provider":"x","model":"m","base_url":"https://host/v1","api_key_env":"X_API_KEY","roles":["frontier"]}]
#
# local_only refuses every model that is not on our own
# network, whatever is configured above.
# LLM_EGRESS_POLICY=external_allowed

# --- SEC fundamentals ---------------------------------------
# Point-in-time quarterly figures from SEC EDGAR join every
# investigation as observations and calculations. EDGAR asks
# each client to identify itself: an app name and a contact.
# Unset, investigations run on news alone and the graph
# records the fundamentals as missing evidence.
# SEC_USER_AGENT=Pythia research you@example.com

# --- Universe -----------------------------------------------
# Pair scans and discovery search data/universe/securities.json
# (Russell 2500 + STOXX 600, ~3,200 securities). Fill the price
# cache once with `make universe`. "off" returns to the small
# hand-written list in UNIVERSE_FILE.
# UNIVERSE_CATALOG=off
# How many of them pair scans and discovery compare (0 = all).
# Large caps first, then the sectors of the book, then the rest.
# Everything stays searchable. Restart after changing the book
# a lot, so its sectors are the ones that come first.
# UNIVERSE_MAX=1000

# --- Replay -------------------------------------------------
# Pin the desk to a past date: later prices and later news do
# not exist. Use it for a recorded, reproducible demo. Run
# `make news` after changing it. Unset means live.
# AS_OF=2026-09-18

# --- News ---------------------------------------------------
# Yahoo Finance and GDELT need no key. Every key below adds a
# provider; without it the provider is simply not used. The
# desk answers from data/cache/news and refreshes behind the
# request, asking each provider only as often as its free
# tier allows (GET /api/news/sources shows what was spent).
# `make news` downloads history from the same providers into
# data/archive/news.
#
# finnhub.io: 60 requests/minute, one year back, US symbols
# FINNHUB_API_KEY=
# eodhd.com: 20 API calls/day and a news request costs 10; covers non-US listings
# EODHD_API_KEY=
# marketaux.com: 100 requests/day, 3 articles per request
# MARKETAUX_API_KEY=
# gnews.io: 100 requests/day, 10 articles per request, about a month back
# GNEWS_API_KEY=
# newsapi.org: 100 requests/day, articles a day late, one month back
# NEWS_API_KEY=
# alphavantage.co: 25 requests/day (ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY is read too)
# ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=
#
# Minutes before a source without a quota of its own (Yahoo,
# SearXNG) is asked about the same ticker again.
# NEWS_CACHE_MINUTES=30
#
# Optional web search, also used by investigations:
# SEARXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888     # after `make search`

# --- Desk ---------------------------------------------------
# On start the desk fills its slow caches in the background
# (prices of the universe, the book's anomalies, post-mortem,
# news), so the first page load does not wait for them.
# `curl :PORT/api/health` shows when it is done. 0 switches it off.
# WARM_ON_START=1
# Its last step re-downloads universe prices older than
# MARKET_CACHE_MINUTES, in the background. 0 leaves that to
# `make universe`.
# UNIVERSE_REFRESH_ON_START=1
BENCHMARK=SPY
REVIEW_DAYS=30
PAIRS_ALPHA=0.05
# Relationships are fitted on 24 months of sessions. beta and
# const stay frozen; the mean and standard deviation a spread is
# judged with are re-estimated every PAIRS_RECALIBRATE_SESSIONS
# sessions from the trailing PAIRS_RECALIBRATION_WINDOW sessions,
# always from data before the session judged (0 = never).
# PAIRS_FORMATION=504
# PAIRS_RECALIBRATE_SESSIONS=21
# PAIRS_RECALIBRATION_WINDOW=252
# Cointegration tests are statsmodels' (adfuller, coint). A scan
# of more than a few dozen tests spreads them over this many
# worker processes; unset, every core; 1 runs them in-process.
# PAIRS_WORKERS=
# A pair is only tested when the daily log returns of its legs
# correlate at least this much over the formation window.
PAIRS_CORR_MIN=0.70
# A looser bar for two names of the same sector. Unset, the one
# bar above applies to every pair.
# PAIRS_CORR_MIN_SAME_SECTOR=0.50
PAIRS_ENTRY=2.0
